- `test/advanced.ts:352-486` — abort queued task does not unpause, shared controller removes all three, explicit id removes correct task, custom `FifoQueue` removal by id, duplicate id removes the right one.
- `test/advanced.ts:488-527` — queued abort listener cleaned up when the task starts running.
- `test/advanced.ts:529-587` — aborting a queued task emits no `error`/`completed`, still resolves `empty`/`idle`, and `onError` does not reject.
- `test/advanced.ts:590-696` — clear removes queued abort listeners (including shared-signal one-listener case), keeps the running task's shared listener, and lets a later shared-signal abort reject only the running task; cleared queued promises reject with `{name:'AbortError', message:'The queue was cleared'}`.
- `test/advanced.ts:725-761` — running abort listeners cleaned up when jobs complete.
- `test/strict.ts:340-370` — aborted queued task does not execute (3 of 4 execute).
- `test/strict.ts:661-689` — `clear()` cancels the pending strict-mode timeout and the cleared task promise rejects with `{name: 'AbortError'}`.
- `test/rate-limit.ts:497-568` — aborting shared-signal waiting tasks does not start them, emits no `error`, and nothing starts later.
- `test/rate-limit.ts:647-669` — `.clear()` or abort in the same tick resolves `onRateLimitCleared`.
- `test/rate-limit.ts:671-739` — aborting one waiting task lets a different-signal task start at window end; a skipped aborted task does not consume the interval slot.
- `test/rate-limit.ts:836-891` — after `.clear()` in the same window, a new task is rate-limited and runs at window end; cleared promise rejects with name `AbortError`.
